From 5d2c2b2d6d77032d116d28e87dab80ae884de417 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:49:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] refactor(ui): tool drawing inks are theme tokens

The tool, holder and profile previews, the library thumbnails, the
tool body page and the refusal and warning text of the tool pages drew
with colour literals and module consts. Eighteen tokens now carry them,
each a theme-file key. Both tables keep the old values, so no pixel
changes. The consts become functions that read the live token.

theme::with_alpha gives a token's own colour at an alpha, read
unmultiplied, for the holder fills; ground_ink::facet_veil uses it too.

The colour-literal guard loses the ten rows of the tool family.

Refs #1120

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
